[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-35558"] :question/problem "Let $W$ be the set of all polynomials in the variable $x\\in R$ with coefficients in $R$ of degree $5$ or greater. Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$W$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$W$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because **$W$ does not contain the zero element.** *\n\nIndeed, the zero polynomial has degree $0$, which is less than $5.$\n\nOn the other hand: \n\n- Addition of polynomials is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- For any polynomial $p(x)$ of degree $5$ (or greater), the corresponding negative polynomial $-p(x)$ has the same degree. $\\,✓$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-106929/selection/4323da32f4d0e343524480efb3fc2e33f66f54e3b33c2db4aac6648792846d8c" :answer/id #uuid "e13ec148-f3af-5f03-8b5f-2dbeeceac2c4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of polynomials is not commutative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106929/selection/0bcdbb5e1d8578fbb302f902f9215efe0f182b4e5bbfcd202fcd22e782901d36" :answer/id #uuid "b8eabd34-2b3b-55a1-96ab-ab60b97e5c23" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106929/selection/0254c053a8fcf9e56483b2456fce38aaf17ebd8281a4ef72b0e22e947931a0b7" :answer/id #uuid "4688d73b-9179-5ae6-ae97-603ba62dfce0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of polynomials is not associative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106929/selection/e1fc478b411592e58e576448691053e9633d1468a76b5b3bd4bf64be4b8fde16" :answer/id #uuid "62aaa84f-a336-5fb0-96dc-f7020990aa8c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1\\cdot p\\ne p$ for some $p\\in Y$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106929/selection/41486ea51f484622f0661e7a8b55a516fd68f7adbeb4f14f3692ec3fc17350d8" :answer/id #uuid "e38ba574-7ad3-5ad2-81ce-e27fc819db61" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of polynomials in $Y$ is not closed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106929/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "91cae22a-4346-52fb-a7f4-10f70ab881db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106929/selection/41486ea51f484622f0661e7a8b55a516fd68f7adbeb4f14f3692ec3fc17350d8" :answer-field/choices ["q-106929/selection/4323da32f4d0e343524480efb3fc2e33f66f54e3b33c2db4aac6648792846d8c" "q-106929/selection/0bcdbb5e1d8578fbb302f902f9215efe0f182b4e5bbfcd202fcd22e782901d36" "q-106929/selection/0254c053a8fcf9e56483b2456fce38aaf17ebd8281a4ef72b0e22e947931a0b7" "q-106929/selection/e1fc478b411592e58e576448691053e9633d1468a76b5b3bd4bf64be4b8fde16" "q-106929/selection/41486ea51f484622f0661e7a8b55a516fd68f7adbeb4f14f3692ec3fc17350d8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106929" :question/id #uuid "4c206776-99db-55ba-ae48-7c0ec7d6d597" :question/math-academy-id "q-106929" :question/problem "Let $Y$ be the set of all polynomials in the variable $x\\in R$ with coefficients in $R$ of degree exactly $2.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because **addition of polynomials in $Y$ is not closed.** *\n\nIndeed, let's consider, for example, the polynomials $p(x)={x}^{2}+x$ and $q(x)=-{x}^{2}.$ Then $p,q\\in Y,$ but \n\n$$\np(x)+q(x)={x}^{2}+x+(-{x}^{2})=x\\notin Y\n$$\n\n because $\\operatorname{deg}⁡(p+q)=1\\ne 2.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- $1\\cdot p=p$ for all $p\\in Y.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of polynomials is associative. $\\,✓$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106929/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106929"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106813/selection/2f5de4dbecac6e017b1b5d03a69c140dea3d55041ace653d0b3882f3d3696c53" :answer/id #uuid "75f11239-8a13-52a6-b25f-87a13580da05" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of $f,g\\in F$ is not commutative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106813/selection/928635fa14fde136889717f60f1f5e20dddac45d7a57211b6756c7fea7b55167" :answer/id #uuid "e1f13a8f-3c54-58b4-97f3-8683bc95d71e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of $f,g\\in F$ is not associative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106813/selection/1989a152de8cc39abbf055134f6d50f07fc2548062b877a862739130df7d2957" :answer/id #uuid "1ce21c01-f17a-54b1-beb0-cac4f6946d6f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of functions in $F$ do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106813/selection/5e9e93c5d9eca5195128e53f5dc8fe23579ae0c47c45acff4b51fe921f13a157" :answer/id #uuid "824101ce-ad6e-5d33-8b0a-2323495b2b6b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in F$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106813/selection/15758073247b21907d3521566bc167120a6985c2929fec117b8927363693cc65" :answer/id #uuid "042dc0fb-357e-59c1-8d04-096ccfbb7570" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$F$ does not contain the zero element" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106813/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1768b600-a256-5baa-8032-a21788f16c7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106813/selection/15758073247b21907d3521566bc167120a6985c2929fec117b8927363693cc65" :answer-field/choices ["q-106813/selection/2f5de4dbecac6e017b1b5d03a69c140dea3d55041ace653d0b3882f3d3696c53" "q-106813/selection/928635fa14fde136889717f60f1f5e20dddac45d7a57211b6756c7fea7b55167" "q-106813/selection/1989a152de8cc39abbf055134f6d50f07fc2548062b877a862739130df7d2957" "q-106813/selection/5e9e93c5d9eca5195128e53f5dc8fe23579ae0c47c45acff4b51fe921f13a157" "q-106813/selection/15758073247b21907d3521566bc167120a6985c2929fec117b8927363693cc65"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106813" :question/id #uuid "1cd61265-dcc6-5f89-bc03-f1168b91584b" :question/math-academy-id "q-106813" :question/problem "Let $F$ be the set of functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$F$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$F$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because **$F$ does not contain the zero element.** *\n\nIndeed, evaluating the zero function $f(x)=0$ at $x=0,$ we have $f(0)=0\\ne \\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of $f,g\\in F$ is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of $f,g\\in F$ is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in F.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of functions satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106813/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106813"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106933/selection/a29949613cd73e7af1d3c653ec985c36c4b83d47dd8e99a1667450b4724c40f4" :answer/id #uuid "b54006c2-3e06-5b4b-ad46-c76fc8f42806" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of functions is not associative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106933/selection/e55795f52c0d0e93eff79a551178375b18905c082b9082558435009d8e152041" :answer/id #uuid "0b19a27a-a3ea-5832-a1a3-b2f087245cb8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$I$ does not contain the zero element" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106933/selection/b995fa6cee691762cad1e47239d32ebacbe46cf3a5779155ece45a65cb734a18" :answer/id #uuid "89be815e-1f63-5f46-9e5e-f1df8575e80c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of functions do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106933/selection/9c279caa6b673c706cd42011414b98049ca7811e50b185c29ff9238347b5513a" :answer/id #uuid "ce898fe8-fd6b-5b52-9017-e65ffe00ec21" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of functions is not commutative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106933/selection/cf84a0be6615cf8b724267d39f017290147872766eceddaea4686d5e27a46450" :answer/id #uuid "4f5e12eb-b8cc-5911-a395-825117509f5e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in I$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106933/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "acf2c2d0-e9ec-5df9-897b-76e64f127228" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106933/selection/e55795f52c0d0e93eff79a551178375b18905c082b9082558435009d8e152041" :answer-field/choices ["q-106933/selection/a29949613cd73e7af1d3c653ec985c36c4b83d47dd8e99a1667450b4724c40f4" "q-106933/selection/e55795f52c0d0e93eff79a551178375b18905c082b9082558435009d8e152041" "q-106933/selection/b995fa6cee691762cad1e47239d32ebacbe46cf3a5779155ece45a65cb734a18" "q-106933/selection/9c279caa6b673c706cd42011414b98049ca7811e50b185c29ff9238347b5513a" "q-106933/selection/cf84a0be6615cf8b724267d39f017290147872766eceddaea4686d5e27a46450"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106933" :question/id #uuid "17d56701-363e-5629-ba43-f0ff54124002" :question/math-academy-id "q-106933" :question/problem "Let $I$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ of the form $f(x)={2}^{ax},$ where $a\\in R.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$I$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$I$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because **$I$ does not contain the zero element.** *\n\nIndeed, $f(x)={2}^{ax}>0$ for all $x\\in R$ for any $a\\in R,$ hence the zero function $z(x)=0\\notin I.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in I.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws.\n$\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is commutative. $\\,✓$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106933/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106933"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94809/selection/caaa05fd4f32fba51daa646cf8cea3ac3859d441512e525b2450f9c96d89f6b3" :answer/id #uuid "dfecf388-51e2-52e2-beb2-c0f9eef7ec6e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$J$ does not contain the element $-z$ for every $z\\in J$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94809/selection/db9098b4114016893d22be6a33318630cffcf928e12f46fbf2ce44ec90277dee" :answer/id #uuid "23c65fa1-1ccd-53df-9697-e8bf7a6bbb51" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition in $J$ is associative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94809/selection/5fe6db46db29182cdb036527e3d93ae724e2a28fad344cb691f9c230159eba35" :answer/id #uuid "33fd80c2-d4b2-5c36-9078-ae6103f2e2ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Addition and scalar multiplication in $J$ satisfy the distributive laws" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94809/selection/0ea14e9744e66eb4c3d880f9ffa24d9296d9127873a45598efc7fed2bdbdc1cb" :answer/id #uuid "39860af3-1b79-5fdc-88d3-f97cfc645329" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "multiplication of $z\\in J$ by real  scalars is not closed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94809/selection/cbe436303b7605b74cded652ff18f0598c91ce0ee211da2cf15889e796b7cc0c" :answer/id #uuid "fd0d5d87-5022-5964-9962-bbe7d80e952d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition  in $J$ is commutative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94809/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "be8584fa-8452-5218-be07-512f0778d847" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94809/selection/0ea14e9744e66eb4c3d880f9ffa24d9296d9127873a45598efc7fed2bdbdc1cb" :answer-field/choices ["q-94809/selection/caaa05fd4f32fba51daa646cf8cea3ac3859d441512e525b2450f9c96d89f6b3" "q-94809/selection/db9098b4114016893d22be6a33318630cffcf928e12f46fbf2ce44ec90277dee" "q-94809/selection/5fe6db46db29182cdb036527e3d93ae724e2a28fad344cb691f9c230159eba35" "q-94809/selection/0ea14e9744e66eb4c3d880f9ffa24d9296d9127873a45598efc7fed2bdbdc1cb" "q-94809/selection/cbe436303b7605b74cded652ff18f0598c91ce0ee211da2cf15889e796b7cc0c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94809" :question/id #uuid "5e96e196-0c41-5ca6-b712-3709509eeb35" :question/math-academy-id "q-94809" :question/problem "Let $J$ be the set of purely imaginary complex numbers, that is, complex numbers of the form  $ai,$ where  $a$ is a nonzero real number. Complete the following sentence: \n\n*$J$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to addition of complex numbers and scalar multiplication of a complex number by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$J$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to addition of complex numbers and scalar multiplication of a complex number by a real number) because **multiplication of $z\\in J$ by real scalars is not closed.** *\n\nFor example, if $\\alpha =0$ and $z=i,$ then $\\alpha \\cdot z=0\\cdot i=0\\notin J.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition in $J$ is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition  in $J$ is commutative.  $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication in $J$ satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- If  $z\\in J$ then $z=ai$ for some $a\\in R.$ Hence, $-z=(-a)i\\in J$   since $-a\\in R.$ $\\,✓$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94809/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94809"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106938/selection/eb8b629ca749d3a3a588c7ede443b3fe5710b22dd0f1debc2ea8614f2bf97529" :answer/id #uuid "2076147d-8933-53a2-bdb8-613d06226d4d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106938/selection/01cbc04e578fa8c2560ec71c32f0249c66c90fa305e1ba7cc92c6fee403dc58b" :answer/id #uuid "46e9f705-09df-5d5a-9c36-b997e0546d99" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106938/selection/e0a423e90a09e73ed8c029421bfd828f82ec1406d4ea59f1c43e151c625f96a2" :answer/id #uuid "599cddd4-d7db-5139-adaa-0ae2f9131ae8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106938/selection/76f23b6ce01bab004c3a79514216736791c83e06fab7d9f09ed7d4c276abe0b2" :answer/id #uuid "8bb61d29-1193-54bf-8920-cb61a6a85227" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106938/selection/0a4994288cee1aabe8966a1a1531e26e48145226e29b564a740a9410bb758e4d" :answer/id #uuid "2fd6f2fa-5ed5-5046-a077-b1c791ae5024" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106938/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8cb8e73b-a644-5ef2-b66f-b49c5ba1f48f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106938/selection/0a4994288cee1aabe8966a1a1531e26e48145226e29b564a740a9410bb758e4d" :answer-field/choices ["q-106938/selection/eb8b629ca749d3a3a588c7ede443b3fe5710b22dd0f1debc2ea8614f2bf97529" "q-106938/selection/01cbc04e578fa8c2560ec71c32f0249c66c90fa305e1ba7cc92c6fee403dc58b" "q-106938/selection/e0a423e90a09e73ed8c029421bfd828f82ec1406d4ea59f1c43e151c625f96a2" "q-106938/selection/76f23b6ce01bab004c3a79514216736791c83e06fab7d9f09ed7d4c276abe0b2" "q-106938/selection/0a4994288cee1aabe8966a1a1531e26e48145226e29b564a740a9410bb758e4d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106938" :question/id #uuid "dd84fbde-b275-5aa2-98b5-041f7a21abda" :question/math-academy-id "q-106938" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n*Given any $x\\in V$, if $y$ is a vector such that $x+y=0$, then $y=-x.$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+y)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ y+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ y+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ y & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+y)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,\\,] \\\\ y+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ y+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ y & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-106938/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106938"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106944/selection/9e8514727248f5b67f046ee5d3463c87a46745f9f426856ba2270470431dc2ed" :answer/id #uuid "dbc3db7a-cc7c-5c43-8f37-ca233f6cf186" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106944/selection/3af39b9899c8aee984ac508208413ae7b69a6ca8795fe7b27228b147889d8176" :answer/id #uuid "0c9b4075-08ac-5f90-92a8-0fe1d20845b9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{A7}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106944/selection/c218effc053382c46a4ada256a5e84c6e1d5947c0f96ab9fc99ce1388d130225" :answer/id #uuid "9da2369d-33f1-59bb-b54b-371eb1833f12" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{A6}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106944/selection/23